* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*    call !acc_os_akpath(data.path, ak.path, err)
*
* A per-OS helper of RESTORE.ACCOUNT (see !acc_archive), called after
* !acc_os_place for a hashed file whose relocated indices lay inside the
* account: sdidx -p refuses an index directory that does not exist yet, so it
* cannot be run on the staged tree.
*
* SUCCESS IS sdidx -q NAMING ak.path, not sdidx -p's exit status: -p prints
* nothing when it works and does not check its own header write
* (gplsrc/sdidx.c, case 'P').  The work is sd-account-archive.ps1 -Mode AkPath.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
subroutine acc_os_akpath(data.path, ak.path, err)
$catalog !acc_os_akpath

   counts = ''
   call !acc_archive('AKPATH', '', data.path : @fm : ak.path, counts, err)
   return
end
